{
  "sn11.5:0.1": "Linked Discourses 11.5 ",
  "sn11.5:0.2": "Chapter One ",
  "sn11.5:0.3": "Victory by Good Speech ",
  "sn11.5:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn11.5:1.2": "“Once upon a time, mendicants, a battle was fought between the gods and the titans. ",
  "sn11.5:1.3": "Then Vepacitti, lord of titans, said to Sakka, lord of gods, ",
  "sn11.5:1.4": "‘Lord of gods, let there be victory by fine words!’ ",
  "sn11.5:1.5": "‘Vepacitti, let there be victory by fine words!’ ",
  "sn11.5:1.6": "Then the gods and the titans appointed a panel of judges, saying, ",
  "sn11.5:1.7": "‘These will understand our good and bad statements.’ ",
  "sn11.5:1.8": "Then Vepacitti, lord of titans, said to Sakka, lord of gods, ",
  "sn11.5:1.9": "‘Lord of gods, recite a verse!’ ",
  "sn11.5:1.10": "When he said this, Sakka said to him, ",
  "sn11.5:1.11": "‘Vepacitti, you are the elder gods here. ",
  "sn11.5:1.12": "Recite a verse.’ ",
  "sn11.5:1.13": "So Vepacitti spoke this verse: ",
  "sn11.5:2.1": "‘Fools would vent even more ",
  "sn11.5:2.2": "if there’s no one to put a stop to them. ",
  "sn11.5:2.3": "So an intelligent person should stop ",
  "sn11.5:2.4": "a fool with forceful punishment.’ ",
  "sn11.5:3.1": "The titans applauded Vepacitti’s verse, while the gods kept silent. ",
  "sn11.5:3.2": "Then Vepacitti said to Sakka, ",
  "sn11.5:3.3": "‘Lord of gods, recite a verse!’ ",
  "sn11.5:3.4": "So Sakka spoke this verse: ",
  "sn11.5:4.1": "‘I think that this is the only way ",
  "s